   "analysis": "BaseGrouper.indices builds the dict from each grouping's raw codes (ping.codes) and self.levels. With sort=False and observed=False, recode_for_groupby gives the codes first-appearance order. result_index_and_ids then calls set_categories(_orig_cats), which puts the levels back in category order. So the codes and the levels use different orderings. BaseGrouper.groups uses result_index_and_ids and is correct. The fix is in BaseGrouper.indices, which should use the consistent result_index and ids. Alternatively the codes could be remapped to the level order.",
